    "id": "Q1",
    "text": "To an AC power supply of 220 V at 50 Hz, a resistor of 20 Ω, a capacitor of reactance 25 Ω and an inductor of reactance 45 Ω are connected in series. The corresponding current in the circuit and the phase angle between the current and the voltage is, respectively: [2025]",
    "options": {
      "A": "15.6 A and 30°",
      "B": "15.6 A and 45°",
      "C": "7.8 A and 30°",
      "D": "7.8 A and 45°"
    },
    "answer": "d",
    "explanation": "XL = 45 W, XC = 25 W, R = 20 W ⇒ I = 220 / √((XL - XC)2 + R2) = 220 / √((45 - 25)2 + 202) ⇒ = 220 / (2√2) = 11 / √2 = 7.779 A ⇒ tan φ = (XL - XC) / R = (45 - 25) / 20 = 1 ⇒ φ = 45°",
